        "id": 1076123
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-12T13:47:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since section_ is a string (most likely the address), can we compare that first?  It seems like if we want an ordering, section would be a natural ordering.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 54,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 54,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "d99a62280ae89a66d4e56a7b8f79d08967c08ca8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "934c1050_dd40170d",
        "filename": "system/gd/storage/adapter_config.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 54,
      "author": {
        "id": 1121403
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-12T21:12:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The structure of the config is\n\nconfig_\n -\u003e section1\n   -\u003e key1\u003dvalue1\n   -\u003e key2\u003dvalue2\n -\u003e section2\n   -\u003e key1\u003dvalue1\n   -\u003e key2\u003dvalue2\nmemory_only_config_\n -\u003e section3\n   -\u003e key1\u003dvalue1\n   -\u003e key2\u003dvalue2\n -\u003e section4\n   -\u003e key1\u003dvalue1\n   -\u003e key2\u003dvalue2\n\nHence, the ranking of section only makes sense when they are within the same config. \n\nOn Android, in most cases, the pointer to config_ and memory_only_config_ are the same for every Device class and section_ should be the only difference. \n\nThe reason why config and memory_only_config are included because we have to compare every member variable of this class.",
      "parentUuid": "c29d8903_190e59a5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 54,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 54,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "d99a62280ae89a66d4e56a7b8f79d08967c08ca8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1350335f_b2186cf2",
